        "problem": "Express $\\frac{37-19x}{(3x+1)(x-4)(3-x)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.",
        "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{37-19x}{(3x+1)(x-4)(3-x)} & =\\frac{A}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{B}{(x-4)}+\\frac{C}{(3-x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(3x+1)(x-4)(3-x)$ gives\n\n$$\n37-19x=A(x-4)(3-x)+B(3x+1)(3-x)+C(3x+1)(x-4).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{1}{3}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}37-19(-\\frac{1}{3}) & =A(-\\frac{1}{3}-4)(3-(-\\frac{1}{3})) \\\\  & +B(3(-\\frac{1}{3})+1)(3-(-\\frac{1}{3})) \\\\  & +C(3(-\\frac{1}{3})+1)(-\\frac{1}{3}-4) \\\\ 37+\\frac{19}{3} & =A(-\\frac{130}{9}) \\\\ \\frac{130}{3} & =A(-\\frac{130}{9}) \\\\ A & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=4$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}37-19(4) & =A(4-4)(3-4) \\\\  & \\,+B(3(4)+1)(3-4) \\\\  & +C(3(4)+1)(x-4) \\\\ 37-76 & =B(-13) \\\\ B & =\\frac{-39}{-13} \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}37-19(3) & =A(3-4)(3-3) \\\\  & \\,+B(3(3)+1)(3-3) \\\\  & +C(3(3)+1)(3-4) \\\\ 37-57 & =C(-10) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-20}{-10} \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{37-19x}{(3x+1)(x-4)(3-x)}=-\\frac{3}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{3}{(x-4)}+\\frac{2}{(3-x)}.\n$$",
